   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The outermost operation is a quotient with numerator \\( e^{\\sin(5x)} \\) and denominator \\( 5^{x} \\), so the quotient rule comes first (equivalently, rewrite \\( f \\) as a product with the factor \\( 5^{-x} \\)).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Exp",
               [
                  "Sin",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     5,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Power",
               5,
               "x"
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "\\( 5^{x} \\) is an exponential function with a constant base, so its derivative is \\( 5^{x} \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)} \\); the power rule does not apply to it.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Power",
               5,
               "x"
            ],
            [
               "Ln",
               5
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The factor \\( e^{\\sin(5x)} \\) is an exponential of \\( \\sin(5x) \\), which is a sine of \\( 5x \\), so apply the chain rule from the outside inward: \\( \\left(e^{\\sin(5x)}\\right)' = 5 e^{\\sin{\\left(5 x \\right)}} \\cos{\\left(5 x \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            5,
            [
               "Exp",
               [
                  "Sin",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     5,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Cos",
               [
                  "Multiply",
                  5,
                  "x"
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Assemble the quotient rule and evaluate at \\( x = 0 \\): \\( f'(0) = 5 - \\ln{\\left(5 \\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Subtract",
            5,
            [
               "Ln",
               5
            ]
         ]
      }
